Syntax: ensoul <opal>

Ensoul calls something into an opal and leaves a soulstone in its place.

The size of the stone decides the size of what answers: five carats to a
level, so a small opal makes a level one stone and only the greatest make a
level ten.  A stone with no carats at all still answers, faintly.

It is paid for in lifeforce, and the price rises with the stone.  Ten
landed calls for every carat, each of them drawing on you at a rate set by
how big the opal is -- which makes a great stone an undertaking rather than
an afternoon.

See also: RITES, BOLSTER, SOULSTONE
